// 007.7 (D35, #52): `Protection` is the dual of `Immunity`: an act whose authority ended still
// takes valid institutional effect for a protected recipient unless an `Unless` condition holds.
Fact person Identified by Agent, Buyer
Bool authorized
Fact notice Identified by person
Fact sold Identified by person
Power sell Actor person Recipient person'
  Holds when authorized()
  Valid when authorized()
  Creates sold(person')
Protection apparent-authority Holder person' For sell
  Unless notice(person')
.
// Agent's authority is gone, Buyer has no notice: unlawful for Agent, valid for Buyer!
?!lawful sell(Agent, Buyer).
?valid sell(Agent, Buyer).
sell(Agent, Buyer).
?sold(Buyer).
// Once Buyer receives notice, protection lifts and a further sale is void:
-sold(Buyer).
+notice(Buyer).
?!valid sell(Agent, Buyer).
sell(Agent, Buyer).
?!sold(Buyer).
